{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788225244,"nonce":"/nADrfX05Yp8Fd1ZXK74onV1eSY=","message":"BUILT AND MERGED (`9219a6d`), acceptance PARTLY proven on the bench — session 11 (`65b03c2`), 2026-08-31. **Not closing**, because one bullet is not demonstrated.\n\n## Proven live, on a bench running the assembly that contains the change (`2a31cb9`, built at `cd9f390`)\n\n- **The gear lands forbidden.** `dev:starter-kit {preset:\"combat\"}` reports `forbidden_stacks: 10`, `not_forbiddable: []`.\n- **Confirmed by a SECOND, INDEPENDENT verb rather than by the kit's own report.** `unforbid` over the kit's rect accepted exactly **10** — `Designator_Unforbid.CanDesignateThing` only accepts a thing that is actually forbidden, so the count is the game's own answer, not ours.\n- **The remedy works, and the state really changed.** A second `unforbid` over the same rect accepted **0**, with all 15 cells reported `not-designatable`.\n- **The obstacle is real and it persists.** Left forbidden and advanced 2500 ticks, all 10 stacks were still there and still forbidden (`unforbid` accepted 10 afterwards) — nothing hauled them away while forbidden, which is the behaviour the issue is about.\n- **Journaled as a dev action.** Journal row `type: dev`, seq 133, payload carrying `forbid: true`, `forbidden_stacks: 10`, `not_forbiddable: 0`, plus the plan — so M1's no-dev-verbs-after-staging invariant still reads off the journal alone.\n- **The other staging verbs question is decided and stated.** `dev:spawn-thing` does NOT follow: its provenance is `Verse/DebugThingPlaceHelper.DebugSpawn`, which forbids nothing — a bare spawn models a thing APPEARING, an arrival is a different fiction. It gains an opt-in `forbid` arg defaulting to `false`, which is how the kit reuses placement rather than reimplementing it. `dev:spawn-pawn`, `dev:finish-research` and `dev:unfog` have nothing to forbid.\n\n## NOT proven, and this is why the issue stays open\n\nAcceptance bullet 2 says `unforbid` clears it **\"and a pawn then picks the gear up — proving the obstacle was real and the remedy works, not just that a flag flipped.\"** After unforbidding and advancing a further 4000 ticks, **no haul job ran** — zero rows mentioning haul in the journal window. The flag flipped; the pickup did not happen. Most likely the bench save has no stockpile the kit's rect can feed, but that is a hypothesis, not a measurement.\n\nThat bullet was written precisely to stop 'a flag flipped' from counting as done, so it would be wrong to close on the flag. What remains is one fixture: a colony with somewhere to haul to.\n\n## Two findings from the build worth keeping\n\n- **`CompForbiddable` is not universal and its absence is SILENT BY DESIGN.** `ForbidUtility.SetForbidden` needs a `ThingWithComps` carrying the comp. `ResourceBase` declares it; `BuildingBase` does not — the kit's own `medical` preset spawns `Bed`, which has no comp anywhere in BedWithQualityBase → BedBase → FurnitureBase → BuildingBase. `warnOnFail: true` makes a miss a `Log.Error` (a red_error, against the zero-red-errors invariant); `warnOnFail: false` makes it a no-op after which `IsForbidden` answers false forever. The game relies on that silence — `DoDropPods` forbids the arriving PAWN in the same group. We take `warnOnFail: false` and then REPORT every miss with its reason.\n- **Two deviations from `DropThingGroupsNear`, both deliberate.** (1) It forbids blind; we ask `Designator_Forbid.CanDesignateThing` first, because that same category test gates the REMEDY `Designator_Unforbid.CanDesignateThing` which the shipped `unforbid` drives — forbidding a Building-with-comp would be a lock with no key. (2) It forbids BEFORE placing; we forbid the placed result, because `CompForbiddable` overrides neither `AllowStackWith` nor `PreAbsorbStack`, so a forbidden stack absorbed into an unforbidden one loses the flag.","files":null}]}